&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;41&quot;&gt;K2 is building the largest and highest-power satellites ever flown, unlocking performance levels previously out of reach across every orbit. Backed by over $1 billion in total funding from leading investors including Altimeter Capital, ICONIQ, Kleiner Perkins, Lightspeed Venture Partners, Redpoint Ventures, and T. Rowe Price — and with over $1 billion in signed contracts across commercial and US government customers, we&#39;re mass-producing the highest-power satellite platforms ever built for missions from LEO to deep space.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;570&quot;&gt;The rise of heavy-lift launch vehicles is shifting the industry from an era of mass constraint to one of mass abundance, and we believe this new era demands a fundamentally different class of spacecraft. Engineered to survive the harshest radiation environments and to fully capitalize on today&#39;s and tomorrow&#39;s massive rockets, K2 satellites deliver unmatched capability at constellation scale and across multiple orbits.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;994&quot;&gt;With multiple launches in 2027 and plans to scale to 100 satellites a year, we&#39;re Building Bigger — helping develop the solar system and build toward a Kardashev Type II (K2) civilization. If you are a motivated individual who thrives in a fast-paced environment and you&#39;re excited about contributing to the success of a high-growth Series D-funded company, we&#39;d love for you to apply.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Our enterprise software team builds the digital backbone that powers K2 Space’s satellite design, manufacturing, and mission operations. We develop tools that connect engineering, production, and mission control into a seamless ecosystem — enabling our hardware to get from concept to orbit faster than ever before.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for engineers who are curious, collaborative, and driven to deliver mission-critical software that helps turn ambitious space projects into reality.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop highly reliable software solutions used across K2 Space — from factory floors to mission control.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create and evolve applications that improve how we design, build, and operate our spacecraft.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with engineers, business partners and leaders across disciplines to understand their challenges and design efficient solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build prototypes to test concepts and validate technical constraints.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop prototypes into working product features.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own full-lifecycle feature development from inception to happy customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Actively contribute to software features and bug fixes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand tradeoffs in competing engineering options and be able to articulate these tradeoffs to senior engineers and contribute to implementation progress.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with customers to drive adoption and make progress on product usability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand priorities communicated by senior staff and work to develop solution with minimal oversight.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to balance being strongly opinionated on tech stack while remaining open-mind and willingness to reevaluate with new data point.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Actively contribute to building a culture of transparency, empathy, integrity and engineering excellence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Actively mentoring other staff members and help team members build good culture and engineering practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in computer science, information technology, mathematics or a STEM discipline or 1-3+ years of professional experience in software engineering.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;1+ years of experience in full stack development, platform engineering or API development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;1+ years of experience with AWS.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;1+ years of in-depth working experience with CI/CD such as GH Actions, Jenkins, Gitlab CI/CD.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;1+ years of in-depth working experience with Git.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;1+ years of in-depth working experience with Docker.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;1+ years of in-depth working experience with Kubernetes (prefer AWS EKS).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working experience with one or more of the following &lt;strong&gt;static typed &lt;/strong&gt;programming languages such as C#.NET, Go, Java.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;1+ years of experience with structured database such as PostgreSQL, SQL Server, Snowflake or similar technologies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;1+ years of experience with unstructured database such as NoSQL, Amazon DynamoDB, MongoDB or similar.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working experience with all aspects of software engineering best practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working experience with REST API or gRPC.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working experience with binary management platforms such as JFrog Artifactory, AWS CodeArtifact or similar technologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with infrastructure orchestration and management tools (Terraform, Ansible, Puppet).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working experience with OAuth 2.0 and OIDC.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to Have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Next.js, React, Angular, or similar frameworks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working experience with TypeScript.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working experience with testing tool such as Cucumber and Cypress.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Foundational knowledge of scalable, high-performance software systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of build systems and package management tools (e.g., Make, Gradle, npm, pip).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation and Benefits:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Base salary range for this role is $123,000&amp;nbsp; $160,000 + equity in the company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Salary will be based on several factors including, but not limited to: knowledge and skills, education, and experience level&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comprehensive benefits package including paid time off, medical/dental/vision/ coverage, life insurance, paid parental leave, and many other perks&lt;/li&gt;
