&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;We’re&amp;nbsp;looking for a stellar Avionics Systems/Test&amp;nbsp;Engineering&amp;nbsp;Intern to join our team for a&amp;nbsp;3&amp;nbsp;month&amp;nbsp;internship. Working closely with our engineers, you will&amp;nbsp;be responsible&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;for&amp;nbsp;system design, analysis,&amp;nbsp;testing&amp;nbsp;and integration of avionics on some of the largest, most powerful, rapidly&amp;nbsp;designed&amp;nbsp;and manufactured satellites.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;You will work hands-on with novel&amp;nbsp;a&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;vionics interfacing, harnessing, instrumentation, RF components, and GNC actuators&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;used across the satellite,&amp;nbsp;while getting exposure to other subsystems within the engineering organization. K2 Space is a highly collaborative&amp;nbsp;environment,&amp;nbsp;and our interns will be encouraged to work with mentors and other team members to execute complex projects.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:240,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
