&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;41&quot;&gt;K2 is building the largest and highest-power satellites ever flown, unlocking performance levels previously out of reach across every orbit. Backed by over $1 billion in total funding from leading investors including Altimeter Capital, ICONIQ, Kleiner Perkins, Lightspeed Venture Partners, Redpoint Ventures, and T. Rowe Price — and with over $1 billion in signed contracts across commercial and US government customers, we&#39;re mass-producing the highest-power satellite platforms ever built for missions from LEO to deep space.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;570&quot;&gt;The rise of heavy-lift launch vehicles is shifting the industry from an era of mass constraint to one of mass abundance, and we believe this new era demands a fundamentally different class of spacecraft. Engineered to survive the harshest radiation environments and to fully capitalize on today&#39;s and tomorrow&#39;s massive rockets, K2 satellites deliver unmatched capability at constellation scale and across multiple orbits.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;994&quot;&gt;With multiple launches in 2027 and plans to scale to 100 satellites a year, we&#39;re Building Bigger — helping develop the solar system and build toward a Kardashev Type II (K2) civilization. If you are a motivated individual who thrives in a fast-paced environment and you&#39;re excited about contributing to the success of a high-growth Series D-funded company, we&#39;d love for you to apply.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Enterprise Information Systems (EIS) team builds the digital backbone behind K2&#39;s satellite design, manufacturing, and mission operations, connecting engineering, production, and mission control so our hardware moves from concept to orbit faster. We&#39;re looking for a Platform Engineer who believes developer experience is a first-class engineering discipline. You&#39;ll build the deployment patterns, guardrails, and tooling that let engineers from many backgrounds, including those building with AI assistance, ship secure, reliable applications with minimal friction.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain golden-path deployment patterns for Amazon EKS, with built-in guardrails that get applications to production faster.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help drive secure, consistent AI adoption across software development, including guardrails, governance, observability, and operational support for AI-assisted workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build automated policies and CI/CD gates that enforce code quality, test coverage, and safe deployments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Integrate end-to-end monitoring, alerting, and SLOs into the platform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track performance and cost (latency budgets, cross-AZ transfer, IP consumption, load balancer efficiency) and act on anomalies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write approachable docs and diagnostics, such as guides, diagrams, and &quot;why can&#39;t this connect?&quot; flows, that shorten support loops.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run proofs of concept on new AI platforms, models, and developer experience tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Learn the manufacturing domain and make complex concerns like service identity and secure communication simple for platform users.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Computer Science or a related field, or equivalent professional experience, plus 2+ years building developer tooling, platforms, or deployment patterns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in at least one of Go, TypeScript, Python, or C#.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience deploying applications on Amazon EKS.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with CI/CD (GitHub Actions or GitLab CI) and disciplined Git workflows (branching, reviews, automated gates).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Practical experience with AI-assisted development and a clear view of its benefits and pitfalls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to Have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Infrastructure as code with Terraform or AWS CDK.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Progressive delivery, such as canary rollouts, and policy-as-code.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Observability experience with metrics, tracing, structured logs, L4/L7 telemetry, and SLI/SLO definition.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building internal developer platforms or golden-path tooling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting manufacturing, aerospace, or other hardware-driven organizations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
