&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a Senior FPGA &amp;amp; Silicon Bring-up Engineer to accelerate the development of next-generation communications ASICs. You will own FPGA prototyping, firmware enablement, first-silicon bring-up, and hardware validation, serving as the bridge between ASIC design, firmware, software, and system integration.&amp;nbsp;This role spans the entire silicon lifecycle from pre-silicon FPGA platforms that enable early hardware/software integration to post-silicon debug, interface validation, and automated test infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop FPGA-based prototypes to enable early ASIC integration, firmware development, and system validation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build hardware platforms that allow software and firmware teams to develop before first silicon.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support first-silicon bring-up, debug, and functional validation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop automated validation infrastructure for silicon characterization and regression testing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Configure and validate digital interfaces including high-speed Ethernet SerDes, SPI, UART, GPIO, and other peripheral interfaces.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop FPGA-based traffic generators, protocol checkers, and test applications for interface validation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Debug issues spanning RTL, firmware, software, FPGA prototypes, and silicon using simulation and laboratory instrumentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate closely with ASIC Design, Verification, Firmware, Software, Systems, and DFT teams to accelerate product development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;BS or MS in Electrical Engineering, Computer Engineering, or related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of FPGA development experience using Verilog/SystemVerilog and AMD/Xilinx FPGA tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of ASIC development and digital system architecture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with FPGA prototyping for ASIC development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with firmware/software enablement and hardware bring-up.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong hardware debugging skills using JTAG, oscilloscopes, logic analyzers, and protocol analyzers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with Python and scripting for automation and test infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to Have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with networking, communications, or satellite systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with embedded processors (ARM or RISC-V).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with hard real-time embedded systems (bare-metal or RTOS).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience validating high-speed digital interfaces, including Ethernet and SerDes protocols, SPI, and UART.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with silicon bring-up using JTAG, logic analyzers, and oscilloscopes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation and Benefits:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
